From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 16:01:50 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Fix: replace Manus Forge storage with local-disk storage for
 hosting off Manus

The app's file storage (uploaded scores, imported PDFs) and its retry-analysis
file fetch went through Manus's private Forge presign service, which is only
reachable from inside a Manus-hosted deployment and returns a 404/500 anywhere
else. Rewrote server/storage.ts and server/_core/storageProxy.ts to read and
write files on local disk (STORAGE_DIR, meant to be a mounted persistent
volume in production) instead. Also hid the "Continue with Manus / Gmail"
button on the login page when VITE_APP_ID/VITE_OAUTH_PORTAL_URL aren't
configured, so the already-working local username/password login is the
primary path when this isn't running on Manus.

TypeScript check, production build, and the pre-existing test suite all pass
(the 3 failures are unrelated tests that require a live DATABASE_URL and a
Scribd session cookie, not present in this environment).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
